00:26:54.640 --> 00:26:55.400
I know.
我知道。

633
00:26:55.720 --> 00:26:57.720
Maybe Kelly needs to make a lot of copies.
也许凯莉需要复印很多东西。

634
00:26:58.000 --> 00:26:59.820
It feels like there's a simple solution.
感觉这有个简单的解决方案。

635
00:27:00.120 --> 00:27:01.300
To the copier problem.
针对复印机的问题。

636
00:27:01.500 --> 00:27:01.620
To the copier.
针对复印机。

637
00:27:01.620 --> 00:27:02.700
No one's realizing.
没人意识到这一点。

638
00:27:02.960 --> 00:27:03.200
Mm-mm.
嗯嗯。

639
00:27:03.440 --> 00:27:07.420
Well, Michael's going to digest all of their ideas and see what comes out the other end.
好吧，迈克尔会消化他们所有的想法，看看最后会得出什么结论。

640
00:27:07.420 --> 00:27:13.800
So coming up at 3 minutes, 56 seconds is a scene, Jenna, that I didn't think I was going
接下来在3分56秒处有一个场景，珍娜，我以为我拍不下去。

641
00:27:13.800 --> 00:27:14.240
to get through.
我以为我们拍不出任何可用的镜头。

642
00:27:14.460 --> 00:27:17.260
I didn't think we would have any usable takes.
我以为我们拍不出任何可用的镜头。

643
00:27:17.500 --> 00:27:22.460
Last week, you talked about that clown painting on the wall in Jim's parents' house that you
上周，你提到了吉姆父母家墙上的那幅小丑画，你们

644
00:27:22.460 --> 00:27:23.580
guys could not get through it.
根本拍不下去。

645
00:27:23.680 --> 00:27:24.100
You were laughing.
你们一直在笑。

646
00:27:24.320 --> 00:27:24.580
Yes.
是的。

647
00:27:24.800 --> 00:27:30.760
This scene with Dwight giving directions to Andy and Angela, that was it for me.
德怀特给安迪和安吉拉指路的这场戏，对我来说就是这样。

648
00:27:30.940 --> 00:27:34.020
Ed and I, we could not get through it.
艾德和我，我们根本拍不下去。

649
00:27:34.220 --> 00:27:36.220
Like, truly, we could not stop laughing.
真的，我们根本停不下来笑。

650
00:27:36.220 --> 00:27:39.540
It's in the bloopers, and I think we got to hear it.
花絮里有，我觉得我们得听听。

651
00:27:39.900 --> 00:27:44.620
You know, lady, last week, I looked at the bloopers to see if I could find any clown
你知道吗，女士，上周我看了花絮，想看看能不能找到任何关于小丑的

652
00:27:44.620 --> 00:27:46.240
painting outtakes.
绘画花絮。

653
00:27:46.380 --> 00:27:46.520
Yeah.
是啊。

654
00:27:46.740 --> 00:27:48.940
I couldn't find them, but I did see this.
我没找到它们，但我看到了这个。

655
00:27:49.120 --> 00:27:50.080
It is so good.
这太棒了。

656
00:27:51.420 --> 00:27:56.780
Just, I feel like some of these directions to Shrewd Farms are a little weird.
只是，我觉得去精明农场的这些指引有点奇怪。

657
00:27:57.520 --> 00:28:02.340
I mean, like, 156 paces from the light red mailbox, make a left.
我是说，比如，从浅红色邮箱走156步，然后左转。

658
00:28:03.520 --> 00:28:05.820
Walk until you hear the beehive.
一直走到你听到蜂巢的声音。

659
00:28:06.220 --> 00:28:10.220
And make a right.
然后右转。

660
00:28:10.460 --> 00:28:14.400
If you are attacked by territorial crows.
如果你被领地意识强的乌鸦攻击了。

661
00:28:15.580 --> 00:28:17.860
I have, this is a really easy.
我有，这真的很简单。

662
00:28:18.480 --> 00:28:22.200
If you smell bear pee, turn the other way.
如果你闻到熊尿味，就往反方向走。

663
00:28:22.520 --> 00:28:29.150
I, if you smell bear pee at any point, abort.
我，如果你在任何时候闻到熊尿味，就放弃吧。

664
00:28:29.550 --> 00:28:31.270
Wait in your car for further instructions.
在车里等待进一步指示。

665
00:28:31.270 --> 00:28:32.570
What's the problem exactly?
到底有什么问题？

666
00:28:37.090 --> 00:28:41.330
The other thing that's so great about this blooper is that you're hearing all those candy bag
这个NG片段最棒的另一件事是，你能听到所有那些糖果袋

667
00:28:41.330 --> 00:28:42.050
alt directions.
备选指引。

668
00:28:42.450 --> 00:28:48.810
Yes, because in the script, the only directions were 156 paces from the light red mailbox, and
是的，因为在剧本里，唯一的指引是从浅红色邮箱走156步，然后

669
00:28:48.810 --> 00:28:49.970
then the one about the bear.
就是关于熊的那一条。

670
00:28:49.970 --> 00:28:52.490
All the rest are candy bag alts.
剩下的全是糖果袋备选台词。

671
00:28:52.670 --> 00:28:56.670
So were they just, because in the clip, you can see that Ed is reading.
所以他们只是，因为在片段里，你可以看到艾德在读。

672
00:28:56.990 --> 00:29:00.130
Were they just handing him pieces of paper with, like, funny directions?
他们只是递给他写着搞笑指引的纸条吗？

673
00:29:00.130 --> 00:29:01.390
They literally did.
他们真的是这样做的。

674
00:29:01.650 --> 00:29:04.610
They handed him a whole paper that were extra directions.
他们递给他整张纸，上面全是额外的指引。

675
00:29:04.630 --> 00:29:06.870
And that's why he was like, I almost had it.
这就是为什么他说，我差点就成功了。

676
00:29:07.950 --> 00:29:11.730
And if you guys watch the bloopers, you'll see that I'm sniffling.
如果你们看花絮，会发现我在吸鼻子。

677
00:29:11.950 --> 00:29:17.290
I am sniffling because it was so cold on set that day that my nose was running.
我在吸鼻子是因为那天片场太冷了，我的鼻涕直流。

678
00:29:17.370 --> 00:29:21.090
And I had a tissue in my hand that I was hiding under the table.
我手里拿着一张纸巾，藏在桌子下面。

679
00:29:21.270 --> 00:29:22.750
It was that cold.
当时就是那么冷。

680
00:29:22.970 --> 00:29:24.690
That used to happen to me all the time.
我以前经常遇到这种情况。

681
00:29:24.830 --> 00:29:26.070
My nose would run on set.
我在片场时鼻涕总会流个不停。

682
00:29:26.230 --> 00:29:26.650
I know.
我知道。

683
00:29:26.910 --> 00:29:30.750
I had my sneezing from the allergies and the runny nose from the cold.
我当时因为过敏在打喷嚏，又因为寒冷在流鼻涕。

684
00:29:30.990 --> 00:29:35.350
Well, I rewatched the scene, and all I can see is me sniffling and trying not to laugh.
好吧，我重看了那场戏，我只能看到自己在吸鼻子，还要努力忍住不笑。

685
00:29:36.530 --> 00:29:38.110
Well, you laughed a lot.
嗯，你笑了很多次。

686
00:29:38.290 --> 00:29:38.670
I did.
确实。

687
00:29:39.290 --> 00:29:41.570
Well, Jenna, we had a fan question about this scene.
好吧，珍娜，我们有一个关于这场戏的粉丝提问。

688
00:29:41.790 --> 00:29:42.710
Allie Joe H.
艾莉·乔·H。

689
00:29:42.850 --> 00:29:43.890
wrote in and said,
来信说，

690
00:29:44.050 --> 00:29:47.870
When Angela and Andy are talking to Dwight, Andy says something about a three-way,
当安吉拉和安迪在和德怀特说话时，安迪提到了关于三人行的事情，

691
00:29:48.050 --> 00:29:50.430
and it looks like Dwight mouths something to Angela.
看起来德怀特对安吉拉说了什么。

692
00:29:50.590 --> 00:29:52.170
Do you remember what he said?
你记得他说了什么吗？

693
00:29:52.430 --> 00:29:56.530
I can tell you in the script, Rain had this stage direction.
我可以告诉你，在剧本里，雷恩有这个舞台指示。

694
00:29:56.810 --> 00:29:57.510
It says,
上面写着，

695
00:29:58.090 --> 00:30:01.830
Dwight rolls his eyes to Angela like, ugh, check out the dummy.
德怀特对安吉拉翻了个白眼，好像在说，呃，看看这个傻瓜。

696
00:30:02.050 --> 00:30:04.370
And Angela doesn't give him anything.
而安吉拉没有给他任何回应。

697
00:30:05.350 --> 00:30:10.310
So I think Rain was sort of mocking Andy in that moment, like looking at me like, ugh, this guy.
所以我认为雷恩当时是在嘲笑安迪，就像看着我说，呃，这家伙。

698
00:30:10.870 --> 00:30:13.270
Coming up, we have a scene that was really, really fun for me.
接下来，我们要看一场对我来说非常非常有趣的戏。

699
00:30:13.430 --> 00:30:19.770
It's the scene in the kitchen between Pam and Jim, where Pam is kind of low-key threatening Jim.
那是帕姆和吉姆在厨房里的戏，帕姆在低调地威胁吉姆。

700
00:30:20.070 --> 00:30:20.510
Yeah.
是啊。

701
00:30:20.790 --> 00:30:21.570
To be on her side.
要站在她这一边。

702
00:30:21.610 --> 00:30:22.610
Not low-key.
不低调。

703
00:30:23.070 --> 00:30:23.650
Full-key?
高调？

704
00:30:23.810 --> 00:30:24.670
Is that an expression?
有这种说法吗？

705
00:30:25.970 --> 00:30:28.030
We had a fan question from Jessica Kay.
我们收到了一位粉丝Jessica Kay的提问。

706
00:30:28.030 --> 00:30:33.710
She would very much like us to discuss Pam's you're on dangerous ground moment, saying, quote,
她非常希望我们聊聊帕姆那句“你现在很危险”的时刻，她说，引用如下：

707
00:30:33.990 --> 00:30:35.590
I was like, damn, Jenna.
我当时心想，天哪，珍娜。

708
00:30:37.970 --> 00:30:42.970
Well, Jessica, we came up with this little moment while we rehearsed the scene.
嗯，Jessica，这个小桥段是我们排练那场戏时想出来的。

709
00:30:43.030 --> 00:30:49.170
So this idea of Pam going over to Jim and going in for a kiss but then pulling back,
帕姆走向吉姆，想要亲吻他，然后又退缩了，

710
00:30:49.630 --> 00:30:52.410
that was something that we did in rehearsal.
这个点子是我们排练时加进去的。

711
00:30:52.710 --> 00:30:54.110
It was not in the script.
剧本里原本没有。

712
00:30:54.130 --> 00:30:56.510
And we just were so tickled.
我们当时觉得特别有意思。

713
00:30:56.650 --> 00:31:01.450
You know those moments when you're rehearsing a scene or you're doing a scene and you come up with this idea
你知道那种感觉吗，当你排练或表演一场戏时，你想出了一个点子，

714
00:31:02.010 --> 00:31:04.530
that just opens it up in this new way?
让整场戏有了全新的展开？

715
00:31:04.690 --> 00:31:05.690
It's so fun.
那真的太有趣了。

716
00:31:05.750 --> 00:31:08.650
And it's so fun to see everyone else realize it, too.
而且看到其他人也意识到这一点，感觉也特别棒。

717
00:31:08.770 --> 00:31:13.490
Because I have to imagine that when Paul Feig saw it, he was like, oh, yes, you have to do that.
因为我猜保罗·费格看到的时候，肯定会说，噢，没错，你们一定要这么演。

718
00:31:13.490 --> 00:31:15.530
Yeah, it was really, really cool.
没错，那真的非常非常酷。

719
00:31:15.790 --> 00:31:18.290
And then we knew we shot this scene firSt.
然后我们知道我们先拍了这场戏。

720
00:31:18.390 --> 00:31:22.290
We were going to mirror it in the tag at the end with Jim.
我们打算在结尾的彩蛋里用吉姆来呼应它。

721
00:31:22.530 --> 00:31:23.770
Oh, it's so good.
噢，太棒了。

722
00:31:23.950 --> 00:31:25.930
And I love Jim's talking head afterward.
我特别喜欢吉姆事后的采访镜头。

723
00:31:26.110 --> 00:31:27.590
He was like, oh, spooky.
他说，噢，真诡异。

724
00:31:28.410 --> 00:31:30.850
You guys were about to head out to Shroop FarMs.
你们当时正准备去施鲁特农场。

725
00:31:31.110 --> 00:31:32.970
There was a deleted driving scene.
有一段被删减的开车戏。

726
00:31:33.190 --> 00:31:33.950
It was so good.
拍得太好了。

727
00:31:34.170 --> 00:31:35.190
There's actually two.
其实有两段。

728
00:31:35.190 --> 00:31:36.530
I'll get to the other one.
我待会儿再说另一段。

729
00:31:36.690 --> 00:31:41.370
Wait, there's a scene of you and Andy and Dwight driving in a car together?
等等，有一场戏是你、安迪和德怀特一起开车的戏？

730
00:31:41.650 --> 00:31:42.130
Two.
两段。

731
00:31:42.390 --> 00:31:42.830
Oh.
噢。

732
00:31:42.830 --> 00:31:44.110
They are bookends.
它们是首尾呼应的。

733
00:31:44.290 --> 00:31:46.810
One going there and then one when we leave.
一段是去的时候，一段是我们离开的时候。

734
00:31:47.070 --> 00:31:47.770
Stop it.
别开玩笑了。

735
00:31:48.010 --> 00:31:48.350
Yes.
是真的。

736
00:31:48.570 --> 00:31:51.230
The one on the way there, Dwight and Angela get into a fight.
去的那段戏里，德怀特和安吉拉吵架了。

737
00:31:51.410 --> 00:31:52.930
Also, Angela's driving.
而且是安吉拉在开车。

738
00:31:53.550 --> 00:31:54.510
That tracks for me.
这很符合她的性格。

739
00:31:54.710 --> 00:31:56.830
Angela's driving and her car is filthy.
安吉拉在开车，她的车脏得要命。

740
00:31:56.990 --> 00:31:58.070
It's like covered in mud.
上面全是泥。

741
00:31:58.170 --> 00:31:58.830
It's so funny.
太搞笑了。

742
00:31:59.210 --> 00:31:59.690
Oh.
噢。

743
00:31:59.910 --> 00:32:00.310
I know.
我知道。

744
00:32:00.430 --> 00:32:04.430
Is that because maybe she's been going out to Shroop Farms recently?
是因为她最近经常去施鲁特农场吗？

745
00:32:04.810 --> 00:32:05.030
Yeah.
没错。

746
00:32:05.550 --> 00:32:06.570
So she's driving.
所以她在开车。

747
00:32:06.830 --> 00:32:09.990
Dwight's in the front and Andy's in the back poking his head through.
德怀特坐在前排，安迪在后排把头探出来。

748
00:32:10.270 --> 00:32:10.570
That's amazing.
太绝了。

749
00:32:10.650 --> 00:32:11.470
For both scenes.
两段戏都是这样。

750
00:32:11.470 --> 00:32:13.610
These scenes were so much fun to film.
拍这些戏真的太好玩了。

751
00:32:13.990 --> 00:32:18.850
On the way there, Angela and Dwight are arguing about centerpieces at the reception.
在去那里的路上，安吉拉和德怀特在争论接待处的餐桌中心装饰品。

752
00:32:19.150 --> 00:32:20.850
Angela wants a fishbowl with a fish in it.
安吉拉想要一个里面有鱼的鱼缸。

753
00:32:21.250 --> 00:32:24.970
Dwight's like, let's put a piranha in it and that will kill the fish and there'll be blood.
德怀特说，放条食人鱼进去，这样它会把鱼吃掉，还会弄得血淋淋的。

754
00:32:25.070 --> 00:32:27.030
And she's like, I don't want blood on my wedding day.
然后她说，我可不想在婚礼当天看到血。

755
00:32:27.190 --> 00:32:29.410
And then he's like, well, I guess I have to reorder the cake.
接着他说，好吧，那我得重新订蛋糕了。

756
00:32:29.410 --> 00:32:30.790
Oh, no.
噢，不。

757
00:32:31.050 --> 00:32:31.790
That's horrible.
太可怕了。

758
00:32:32.230 --> 00:32:32.710
I know.
我知道。

759
00:32:32.830 --> 00:32:33.630
What is this cake?
这是什么蛋糕？

760
00:32:33.830 --> 00:32:34.950
And Andy's like, you too.
安迪说，你也是。

761
00:32:35.430 --> 00:32:36.630
That is on the DVD.
那段在DVD里。

762
00:32:36.950 --> 00:32:42.210
The other one isn't on the DVD, but I'm going to share it later because it's when they're leaving Shroop FarMs.
另一段不在DVD里，但我之后会分享出来，那是他们离开施鲁特农场的时候。

763
00:32:42.210 --> 00:32:52.210
When Dwight is giving Andy and Angela a tour of Shroop Farms, they get into another discussion about, I guess, on theme with blood.
当德怀特带安迪和安吉拉参观施鲁特农场时，他们又讨论起了关于血的话题，我想这大概是主题的一部分。

764
00:32:52.210 --> 00:32:53.710
They're talking about the slaughter.
他们在谈论屠宰的事。

765
00:32:53.950 --> 00:32:56.690
Do they really have to slaughter the entrees on the day of the wedding?
他们真的非得在婚礼当天屠宰主菜吗？

766
00:32:57.010 --> 00:32:57.410
Yeah.
是的。

767
00:32:57.670 --> 00:32:59.010
I mean, yeah.
我是说，没错。

768
00:32:59.010 --> 00:32:59.930
I know.
我知道。

769
00:33:00.670 --> 00:33:03.530
And Andy gets Dwight to not do it the day of the wedding.
后来安迪说服了德怀特不要在婚礼当天屠宰。

770
00:33:03.770 --> 00:33:05.490
And then Andy's like, what's that smell?
然后安迪问，那是什么味道？

771
00:33:05.930 --> 00:33:06.610
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

772
00:33:06.690 --> 00:33:07.210
I'm so Southern.
我太南方人了。

773
00:33:07.330 --> 00:33:07.850
Did you hear that?
你听到了吗？

774
00:33:08.050 --> 00:33:08.310
Smell.
味道。

775
00:33:08.470 --> 00:33:09.290
What's that smell?
那是什么味道？

776
00:33:09.490 --> 00:33:10.650
It's a vowel before an L.
那是L前面的元音。

777
00:33:10.810 --> 00:33:11.530
I can't do it.
我做不到。

778
00:33:12.430 --> 00:33:14.110
And Angela goes, manure.
安吉拉说，是粪肥。

779
00:33:14.370 --> 00:33:15.150
Get rid of it.
把它弄走。

780
00:33:15.750 --> 00:33:18.350
We had a lot of fan questions about the manure.
我们收到了很多粉丝关于粪肥的问题。

781
00:33:18.610 --> 00:33:19.210
Oh, yeah?
噢，是吗？

782
00:33:19.350 --> 00:33:19.910
Like a lot.
非常多。

783
00:33:20.130 --> 00:33:22.710
Everybody wanted to know, was it real manure?
大家都想知道，那是真的粪肥吗？

784
00:33:23.530 --> 00:33:24.570
No, it was not.
不，不是。

785
00:33:24.690 --> 00:33:26.770
It was made by Phil Shea.
那是菲尔·谢伊做的。

786
00:33:26.770 --> 00:33:29.810
Hey, that was Phil Shea's job that day, make fakie manure.
嘿，那天菲尔·谢伊的工作就是制作假粪肥。

787
00:33:30.090 --> 00:33:31.230
And how did he do it?
他是怎么做的？

788
00:33:31.430 --> 00:33:36.230
He mixed mostly oatmeal, a little bit of sand, and some food coloring.
他混合了燕麦片、一点沙子和一些食用色素。

789
00:33:36.510 --> 00:33:37.970
Well, it looks like manure.
嗯，看起来确实像粪肥。

790
00:33:38.210 --> 00:33:38.670
It does.
确实。

791
00:33:39.090 --> 00:33:40.190
Good job, Phil Shea.
干得好，菲尔·谢伊。

792
00:33:40.750 --> 00:33:49.850
Lee Eisenberg shared with me that his most vivid memory of shooting this episode was how hot it was at Shroop FarMs.
李·艾森伯格跟我分享说，他拍摄这一集时最深刻的记忆就是施鲁特农场当时有多热。

