00:35:58.170 --> 00:35:58.490
Yes.
是的。

841
00:35:58.750 --> 00:36:03.590
So my mom and my sister, they loved to go to the outlets at Lake Ozark, Missouri.
我妈和我姐，她们特别喜欢去密苏里州欧扎克湖的奥特莱斯。

842
00:36:04.130 --> 00:36:10.030
All growing up, we would go to this cabin in Lake of the Ozarks in the summer, and they would head out to the outlets.
我从小到大，夏天我们都会去欧扎克湖的一个小屋，她们就会去奥特莱斯。

843
00:36:10.170 --> 00:36:11.250
I'm not a shopper person.
我不是个爱逛街的人。

844
00:36:11.250 --> 00:36:12.590
I'm like, I'm going to stay back.
我会说，我就留在这儿吧。

845
00:36:12.630 --> 00:36:14.290
I'm going to sit on the dock and read a book.
我要坐在码头上看书。

846
00:36:14.290 --> 00:36:16.570
Oh, I would be hitting those outlets with them.
噢，我肯定会跟她们一起去逛那些奥特莱斯。

847
00:36:16.590 --> 00:36:17.890
I know you would.
我知道你会的。

848
00:36:18.550 --> 00:36:23.710
Especially if there was, like, one of those pretzel shops, and I could get a pretzel while we shopped.
特别是如果那里有那种卖椒盐卷饼的店，我可以在逛街的时候买个卷饼吃。

849
00:36:23.710 --> 00:36:25.050
Of course there's a pretzel shop.
当然会有卖椒盐卷饼的店。

850
00:36:25.250 --> 00:36:25.710
Of course.
当然。

851
00:36:25.970 --> 00:36:27.350
Give me that cinnamon pretzel.
给我来个肉桂味的椒盐卷饼。

852
00:36:27.490 --> 00:36:27.830
Yes.
是的。

853
00:36:28.150 --> 00:36:38.350
So you know how nowadays they have those haul videos on YouTube where people go shopping, and they just take things out of their bag, and they show you their haul?
你知道现在YouTube上很流行那种“购物开箱”视频吗？就是人们去购物，然后把东西从袋子里拿出来，展示他们的战利品？

