01:01:33.680 --> 01:01:36.760
And Kevin goes, he's a genius.
凯文就说，他真是个天才。

1406
01:01:37.180 --> 01:01:43.140
Oscar says, okay, Michael, what's 15% of $200?
奥斯卡说，好吧，迈克尔，200美元的15%是多少？

1407
01:01:43.560 --> 01:01:45.060
And then Michael doesn't know.
结果迈克尔答不上来。

1408
01:01:45.300 --> 01:01:50.540
That little bit of Kevin thinking that Michael is a math genius in that moment.
凯文在那一刻觉得迈克尔是数学天才，那个小桥段很有趣。

1409
01:01:50.820 --> 01:01:54.340
Paul Feek said him and his wife, Lori, love that little bit.
保罗·菲克说他和妻子洛里很喜欢那个小桥段。

1410
01:01:54.480 --> 01:01:55.880
And that they do that bit.
而且他们还会模仿那个桥段。

1411
01:01:56.060 --> 01:01:59.380
That like, if someone says something, they'll be like, he's a genius.
就像如果有人说了什么，他们就会说，他真是个天才。

1412
01:01:59.980 --> 01:02:01.140
Oh, they do Kevin.
哦，他们模仿的是凯文。

1413
01:02:01.540 --> 01:02:02.460
That's their little bit.
那是他们的小把戏。

1414
01:02:02.460 --> 01:02:07.200
But all of this leads to a very big smooch.
但这一切都引出了一个非常大的吻。

1415
01:02:07.980 --> 01:02:10.800
Andy and Dwight and Angela have returned to the office.
安迪、德怀特和安吉拉回到了办公室。

1416
01:02:11.280 --> 01:02:11.680
Yeah.
没错。

1417
01:02:11.960 --> 01:02:15.020
And once you piss Angela off, she's going to dig in her heels.
一旦你惹恼了安吉拉，她就会变得非常固执。

1418
01:02:15.240 --> 01:02:15.580
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1419
01:02:15.740 --> 01:02:22.080
And she's going to make a very public show to Dwight that she has chosen once again Andy over him.
她会当众向德怀特展示，她再次选择了安迪而不是他。

1420
01:02:22.480 --> 01:02:22.720
Yeah.
没错。

1421
01:02:22.720 --> 01:02:27.460
So Andy is eating a tuna sandwich that he's real proud of.
所以安迪正在吃一个他引以为傲的金枪鱼三明治。

1422
01:02:27.560 --> 01:02:29.820
He wants Jim to know, tuna, I'm eating tuna.
他想让吉姆知道，金枪鱼，我在吃金枪鱼。

1423
01:02:30.100 --> 01:02:34.900
And Angela marches across the bullpen and kisses him.
然后安吉拉穿过办公区，吻了他。

1424
01:02:35.140 --> 01:02:35.680
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1425
01:02:35.880 --> 01:02:37.800
He's leaning back in his chair.
他向后靠在椅子上。

1426
01:02:38.040 --> 01:02:41.840
She lays on his lap and grabs his face.
她坐在他的腿上，捧住他的脸。

1427
01:02:42.320 --> 01:02:44.540
Do you know what the stage direction was for this kiss?
你知道这场吻戏的剧本说明是什么吗？

1428
01:02:44.740 --> 01:02:45.360
Read it.
读一下。

1429
01:02:45.360 --> 01:02:51.660
Angela kisses Andy with a passion we haven't seen since Jim and Pam in Casino Night.
安吉拉以一种自《赌场之夜》中吉姆和帕姆以来我们从未见过的热情吻了安迪。

1430
01:02:51.860 --> 01:02:52.280
I know.
我知道。

1431
01:02:52.460 --> 01:02:53.000
I read that.
我读过那个。

1432
01:02:55.120 --> 01:02:57.660
We had a lot of questions about this scene, though, Angela.
不过，安吉拉，我们对这场戏有很多疑问。

1433
01:02:58.040 --> 01:02:59.860
Oh, well, I bet I have some stories for you.
哦，好吧，我敢说我有一些故事要讲给你们听。

1434
01:03:00.220 --> 01:03:06.240
Dory C and Amanda C both want to know, did Ed actually have tuna in his mouth when you kissed him?
多里·C和阿曼达·C都想知道，当你吻他的时候，埃德嘴里真的有金枪鱼吗？

1435
01:03:06.240 --> 01:03:07.020
Yes.
是的。

1436
01:03:07.340 --> 01:03:07.720
Oh!
哦！

1437
01:03:08.500 --> 01:03:10.180
That was part of the joke.
那是笑话的一部分。

1438
01:03:10.600 --> 01:03:18.840
Lee and Jean, who wrote this episode, they thought it would be very funny if Andy was eating something gross when I had to go kiss him.
编写这一集的李和简认为，如果安迪在我要去吻他的时候吃些恶心的东西会非常有趣。

1439
01:03:18.940 --> 01:03:22.900
And that's why he has that line, look, tuna, tuna fish sandwich, just like you.
这就是为什么他有那句台词，看，金枪鱼，金枪鱼三明治，就像你一样。

1440
01:03:23.060 --> 01:03:28.960
Because they really wanted to make sure the audience knew he was eating this smelly tuna fish sandwich.
因为他们真的想确保观众知道他正在吃这个味道很大的金枪鱼三明治。

1441
01:03:29.600 --> 01:03:34.380
And I was supposed to go over and we're supposed to have this huge kiss while he has tuna fish in his mouth.
我本该走过去，我们本该在嘴里有金枪鱼的情况下进行这个大大的吻。

1442
01:03:34.380 --> 01:03:36.740
And then you see me get up and I wipe my mouth.
然后你看到我起身，擦了擦嘴。

1443
01:03:36.960 --> 01:03:37.240
Yeah.
没错。

1444
01:03:37.800 --> 01:03:38.620
Ed was so sweet.
埃德真是太贴心了。

1445
01:03:38.820 --> 01:03:42.500
He said, Angela, I am going to hold my lips together.
他说，安吉拉，我会把嘴唇闭紧。

1446
01:03:42.720 --> 01:03:43.840
I'm going to take a deep breath.
我会深吸一口气。

1447
01:03:44.060 --> 01:03:45.720
I'm going to take a bite of the tuna fish sandwich.
我会咬一口金枪鱼三明治。

1448
01:03:45.880 --> 01:03:52.300
And then I am going to purse my lips together and not open them at all because I don't want you to get any of this tuna fish.
然后我会把嘴唇紧紧抿住，一点也不张开，因为我不想让你沾到任何金枪鱼。

1449
01:03:52.500 --> 01:03:54.720
I was like, oh, Ed, that is so sweet.
我说，哦，埃德，你真是太贴心了。

1450
01:03:55.220 --> 01:03:59.240
And so we literally did, you know, what we call like grandparent kissing.
所以我们实际上做了我们称之为祖父母式的亲吻。

1451
01:03:59.940 --> 01:04:00.920
You're just like, mm.
就像这样，嗯。

1452
01:04:02.160 --> 01:04:04.860
He did not open his lips for a second.
他一秒钟都没有张开嘴。

1453
01:04:05.040 --> 01:04:09.900
And they really wanted me to sort of have this long kiss, right?
他们真的很想让我来个长吻，对吧？

1454
01:04:10.060 --> 01:04:10.280
Yeah.
没错。

1455
01:04:10.420 --> 01:04:11.340
And I was in control.
而且当时是我在主导。

1456
01:04:11.340 --> 01:04:14.700
I was the one that grabbed him and then I was the one that released him.
是我抓住了他，也是我放开了他。

1457
01:04:14.880 --> 01:04:18.360
And I remember one time they were like, can you sell it a little bit more?
我记得有一次他们说，你能再投入一点吗？

1458
01:04:18.460 --> 01:04:19.940
Can you make it a little bit bigger of a moment?
你能让这一刻显得更浓烈一点吗？

1459
01:04:20.220 --> 01:04:22.520
And poor Ed, the minute we broke apart, he went.
可怜的埃德，我们刚一分开，他就……

1460
01:04:23.400 --> 01:04:25.240
Oh, because he hadn't been breathing?
噢，是因为他一直没呼吸吗？

1461
01:04:25.240 --> 01:04:29.520
He was holding his breath with a big bite of tuna fish sandwich in his mouth.
他嘴里塞着一大口金枪鱼三明治，一直憋着气呢。

1462
01:04:29.840 --> 01:04:31.020
Here's my question.
我有疑问。

1463
01:04:31.360 --> 01:04:33.720
Couldn't Phil have made fakie tuna fish?
菲尔就不能弄点假的金枪鱼吗？

1464
01:04:34.120 --> 01:04:35.020
I don't know.
我不知道。

1465
01:04:35.120 --> 01:04:35.980
Would that have been better?
那样会不会好一点？

1466
01:04:36.320 --> 01:04:37.340
I don't know.
我不知道。

1467
01:04:37.480 --> 01:04:38.960
I mean, what could it have been?
我是说，那还能是什么呢？

1468
01:04:39.320 --> 01:04:39.960
I don't know.
我不知道。

1469
01:04:40.020 --> 01:04:43.640
You could have maybe, I mean, whatever it is, it's going to be mayo based.
你或许可以，我是说，不管是什么，肯定都是蛋黄酱底的。

1470
01:04:43.920 --> 01:04:45.740
But it could have been chopped up chicken.
但可以是切碎的鸡肉啊。

1471
01:04:46.380 --> 01:04:47.400
That's still gross.
那还是很恶心。

1472
01:04:47.880 --> 01:04:49.060
But it's not as stinky.
但没那么臭。

1473
01:04:49.420 --> 01:04:50.060
It's true.
确实。

1474
01:04:50.380 --> 01:04:51.940
But Ed was a true gentleman.
不过埃德真是位绅士。

1475
01:04:52.240 --> 01:04:53.860
He kept his mouth closed.
他一直闭着嘴。

1476
01:04:54.200 --> 01:04:57.020
I didn't get any tuna fish on my person.
我身上一点金枪鱼都没沾到。

1477
01:04:57.640 --> 01:05:02.640
And you guys, when my character stands up and says, and now I have a legal issue to attend to,
还有各位，当我的角色站起来说“现在我有个法律问题要处理”时，

1478
01:05:02.820 --> 01:05:05.900
I actually had a big speech that got deleted.
其实我原本有一大段台词被删掉了。

1479
01:05:06.100 --> 01:05:06.500
Really?
真的吗？

1480
01:05:06.800 --> 01:05:07.120
Yes.
是的。

1481
01:05:07.260 --> 01:05:11.580
And I was so nervous to do it because it was one of those moments where I had a speech in the bullpen
我当时紧张得要命，因为那是那种需要在办公区发表长篇大论的时刻，

1482
01:05:11.580 --> 01:05:12.900
with everyone looking at me.
所有人都盯着我看。

1483
01:05:13.300 --> 01:05:16.980
This is how the script described everyone reacting to the kiss.
剧本里是这样描述大家对那个吻的反应的。

1484
01:05:16.980 --> 01:05:18.420
And my speech after.
以及我之后的那段演讲。

1485
01:05:18.800 --> 01:05:18.900
Okay.
好的。

1486
01:05:20.020 --> 01:05:21.460
Everyone watches with disguSt.
每个人都一脸嫌弃地看着。

1487
01:05:22.540 --> 01:05:24.060
Dwight's eyes go wide.
德怀特瞪大了眼睛。

1488
01:05:24.520 --> 01:05:25.760
Angela pulls away.
安吉拉转过头去。

1489
01:05:26.120 --> 01:05:28.640
Andy continues to chew and then swallows the bite.
安迪继续咀嚼，然后咽下了那一口。

1490
01:05:29.360 --> 01:05:32.340
Angela wipes her mouth and hears the speech.
安吉拉擦了擦嘴，听着那段演讲。

1491
01:05:32.800 --> 01:05:36.520
I would marry you during an earthquake in the middle of a tornado.
就算是在地震中，在龙卷风中心，我也愿意嫁给你。

1492
01:05:36.880 --> 01:05:40.400
I would marry you in the front row of an Elton John concert.
就算是在埃尔顿·约翰演唱会的第一排，我也愿意嫁给你。

1493
01:05:40.700 --> 01:05:43.140
I don't care how terrible a place it is.
我不在乎那地方有多糟糕。

1494
01:05:43.280 --> 01:05:44.880
I just want to be with you.
我只想和你在一起。

1495
01:05:45.740 --> 01:05:47.800
Now, I have a legal matter to clear up.
现在，我有一桩法律事务要处理。

1496
01:05:49.140 --> 01:05:50.800
Not an Elton John fan.
看来不是埃尔顿·约翰的粉丝。

1497
01:05:51.620 --> 01:05:52.020
Clearly.
显而易见。

1498
01:05:52.500 --> 01:05:53.300
Clearly not.
显然不是。

1499
01:05:54.540 --> 01:05:56.720
But yeah, so I had that speech I had to do.
总之，我当时得发表那段演讲。

1500
01:05:56.920 --> 01:05:58.480
And they gave me a few alts, you know.
他们还给了我几个备选方案，你知道的。

1501
01:05:58.620 --> 01:06:00.260
And I was really nervous.
我当时真的非常紧张。

1502
01:06:00.260 --> 01:06:03.640
But all that made it in was, now I have a legal matter to clear up.
但最终保留下来的只有：现在我有一桩法律纠纷要处理。

1503
01:06:03.720 --> 01:06:07.040
And I actually think that was a good edit because the kiss was enough.
而且我确实认为那是个不错的剪辑，因为那个吻已经足够了。

1504
01:06:07.200 --> 01:06:07.380
Yeah.
没错。

1505
01:06:07.380 --> 01:06:07.920
Right?
对吧？

1506
01:06:08.080 --> 01:06:11.280
That was enough of like shoving it in Dwight's face.
那样就已经足够让德怀特难堪了。

1507
01:06:11.440 --> 01:06:12.820
I didn't need to make this speech.
我没必要发表那番演讲。

1508
01:06:13.020 --> 01:06:14.760
But yes, no tuna.
但确实，没有金枪鱼。

1509
01:06:15.020 --> 01:06:15.700
Thank you, Ed.
谢谢你，埃德。

1510
01:06:16.000 --> 01:06:18.800
Very different from a kiss with Rain, who.
这和跟雷恩接吻完全不同，他。

1511
01:06:19.040 --> 01:06:21.780
Actually was eating tuna in real life.
现实生活中其实正在吃金枪鱼。

1512
01:06:22.180 --> 01:06:24.840
Backstage for no reason at all.
在后台，毫无理由地。

1513
01:06:25.000 --> 01:06:25.800
Knowing he has.
明知他有。

1514
01:06:25.860 --> 01:06:26.540
Before a kissing scene.
在吻戏之前。

1515
01:06:26.560 --> 01:06:26.760
Yes.
是的。

1516
01:06:26.980 --> 01:06:32.200
That or drinking coffee while eating like an everything bagel that had onions on it.
要么就是一边喝咖啡，一边吃那种加了洋葱的全料贝果。

1517
01:06:32.360 --> 01:06:32.540
Yeah.
没错。

1518
01:06:32.940 --> 01:06:33.360
Different.
不一样。

1519
01:06:33.720 --> 01:06:34.240
Very different.
非常不一样。

1520
01:06:34.440 --> 01:06:34.920
Approaches.
处理方式。

1521
01:06:37.980 --> 01:06:42.140
This whole copier chair thing is going to wrap up.
关于复印机和椅子的整件事即将收尾。

1522
01:06:42.280 --> 01:06:45.060
The employees are going to confront Michael in his office.
员工们要去办公室找迈克尔对质。

1523
01:06:45.060 --> 01:06:47.480
And he basically tells them, you know what?
他基本上对他们说，你们知道吗？

1524
01:06:47.640 --> 01:06:48.620
You decide.
你们自己决定吧。

1525
01:06:49.040 --> 01:06:52.560
You all have to agree or else I'm taking the bonus.
你们必须达成一致，否则我就拿走奖金。

1526
01:06:52.560 --> 01:06:55.820
Because he kind of thinks like there's no way that's going to happen, right?
因为他觉得这根本不可能发生，对吧？

1527
01:06:56.080 --> 01:06:57.760
Of course he thinks there's no way.
他当然觉得不可能。

1528
01:06:57.880 --> 01:06:59.040
He thinks he got them.
他以为他拿捏住他们了。

1529
01:06:59.200 --> 01:07:01.560
They very quickly decide to get the chairs.
结果他们很快就决定要椅子了。

1530
01:07:01.920 --> 01:07:03.860
He was like, son of a.
他当时就像是，该死的。

1531
01:07:03.860 --> 01:07:05.740
Well, he actually says mother.
嗯，他其实说的是他妈的。

1532
01:07:06.020 --> 01:07:06.860
Yeah, he does.
没错，他说了。

1533
01:07:07.120 --> 01:07:07.440
F.
F开头那个词。

1534
01:07:08.220 --> 01:07:10.400
Was he putting sugar in his Diet Coke?
他是在往健怡可乐里加糖吗？

1535
01:07:10.480 --> 01:07:11.120
He was.
他确实加了。

1536
01:07:11.360 --> 01:07:11.500
Yeah.
没错。

1537
01:07:11.580 --> 01:07:12.660
He wanted to sweeten it.
他想让它变甜一点。

1538
01:07:12.900 --> 01:07:13.620
Oh, my Lord.
噢，天哪。

1539
01:07:15.320 --> 01:07:17.700
The whole thing kind of ends with Michael.
整件事以迈克尔收场。

1540
01:07:17.760 --> 01:07:19.180
He has a talking head.
他有一个单人访谈。

1541
01:07:19.180 --> 01:07:20.600
He wants you to know what he learned.
他想让你知道他学到了什么。

1542
01:07:20.920 --> 01:07:21.920
What did he learn?
他学到了什么？

1543
01:07:22.140 --> 01:07:25.700
He learned that his team is faster at making a decision than he thought.
他学到他的团队做决定的速度比他想象的要快。

1544
01:07:25.940 --> 01:07:26.180
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1545
01:07:26.180 --> 01:07:31.860
He also learned you should never buy a fur coat with a credit card until you actually have the money to pay for it.
他还学到，在真正有钱支付之前，永远不要用信用卡买皮草大衣。

1546
01:07:32.020 --> 01:07:34.020
Michael, why in the world are you buying a fur coat?
迈克尔，你到底为什么要买皮草大衣？

1547
01:07:34.160 --> 01:07:35.280
You are never going to wear it.
你根本就不会穿它。

1548
01:07:35.640 --> 01:07:37.360
It's ridiculous looking.
看起来太荒唐了。

1549
01:07:37.640 --> 01:07:38.040
Yes.
是的。

1550
01:07:38.320 --> 01:07:41.060
He's just like a kid that gets money and doesn't know what to do with it.
他就像个拿到钱却不知道该怎么花的孩子。

1551
01:07:41.140 --> 01:07:45.740
In his mind, that's, I don't know, fancy luxury or something?
在他看来，那是什么，高级奢华之类的东西？

1552
01:07:45.860 --> 01:07:46.020
Yeah.
是啊。

1553
01:07:46.200 --> 01:07:47.700
Fancy people have those or something.
有钱人或者什么人才会有那种东西。

1554
01:07:47.880 --> 01:07:48.580
I guess so.
我想也是。

1555
01:07:48.580 --> 01:07:54.340
The third thing he learned is that people think it's cool to throw fake blood on you as you leave Burlington Coat Factory.
他学到的第三件事是，人们觉得在你离开伯灵顿外套工厂时往你身上泼假血很酷。

1556
01:07:55.220 --> 01:08:00.200
So he has a ruined fur coat that he bought on credit.
所以他有一件赊账买来的皮草大衣被毁了。

1557
01:08:00.360 --> 01:08:01.080
That he can't afford.
而且他还买不起。

1558
01:08:01.460 --> 01:08:01.740
Yeah.
是啊。

1559
01:08:01.940 --> 01:08:03.240
That's how his day ended.
他的一天就是这样结束的。

1560
01:08:03.480 --> 01:08:03.680
Yeah.
是啊。

1561
01:08:05.360 --> 01:08:07.940
Jim and Pam's day is going to end with a truce.
吉姆和帕姆的一天将以休战告终。

1562
01:08:08.160 --> 01:08:10.700
But, oh, can you make me three copies of this?
但是，哦，你能帮我复印三份这个吗？

1563
01:08:10.800 --> 01:08:11.500
I'm just kidding.
我开玩笑的。

1564
01:08:11.600 --> 01:08:12.320
I need four.
我需要四份。

1565
01:08:12.760 --> 01:08:14.320
Is this Jim sass?
这是吉姆式的调侃吗？

1566
01:08:14.540 --> 01:08:16.160
Oh, that's some Jim sass.
哦，这确实是吉姆式的调侃。

1567
01:08:16.400 --> 01:08:18.200
I have one final question for you.
我最后还有一个问题要问你。

1568
01:08:18.200 --> 01:08:18.660
So, yes.
所以，是的。

1569
01:08:19.040 --> 01:08:21.420
Would you be team copier or team chair?
你会选复印机派还是椅子派？

1570
01:08:22.180 --> 01:08:22.900
Team chair.
椅子派。

1571
01:08:23.420 --> 01:08:24.380
What would you be?
你会选什么？

1572
01:08:24.940 --> 01:08:25.600
Team chair.
椅子派。

1573
01:08:26.260 --> 01:08:26.480
Yeah.
是啊。

1574
01:08:26.800 --> 01:08:29.340
Team copier doesn't even make any sense to me, frankly.
坦白说，复印机派对我来说根本说不通。

1575
01:08:29.700 --> 01:08:32.300
I mean, I would just suffer through a crappy machine.
我的意思是，我宁愿忍受一台烂机器。

1576
01:08:32.440 --> 01:08:38.820
How many times have you worked in an office where either the fax machine, I know I'm a dinosaur, or the copier didn't work great.
你在办公室工作时，传真机——我知道我是老古董了——或者复印机不好用，这种情况你遇到过多少次？

1577
01:08:38.980 --> 01:08:41.200
But a chair, that's like your tailbone.
但椅子，那可是关乎你的尾骨。

1578
01:08:41.360 --> 01:08:42.180
That's your spine.
关乎你的脊椎。

1579
01:08:42.360 --> 01:08:43.080
That's your butt.
关乎你的屁股。

1580
01:08:43.420 --> 01:08:45.020
Is anyone team copier?
有人选复印机派吗？

1581
01:08:45.140 --> 01:08:47.380
Can we put a poll in Office Ladies Pod today?
我们今天能在《办公室女士》播客里发起投票吗？

1582
01:08:47.380 --> 01:08:47.720
Yes.
可以。

1583
01:08:48.000 --> 01:08:49.020
I'm so curious.
我太好奇了。

1584
01:08:49.440 --> 01:08:51.040
I'll put a poll, and we'll see.
我会发起投票，我们拭目以待。

1585
01:08:51.240 --> 01:08:51.920
We want to see.
我们想看看结果。

1586
01:08:52.180 --> 01:08:55.180
Well, you guys, that was Spend the Surplus.
好了，各位，以上就是《花掉盈余》这一集的内容。

1587
01:08:55.600 --> 01:08:58.020
And also, Angela's birthday.
还有安吉拉的生日。

1588
01:08:58.340 --> 01:08:58.620
Hey!
嘿！

1589
01:08:59.380 --> 01:08:59.620
Woo!
呜！

1590
01:08:59.840 --> 01:09:00.060
Woo!
呜！

1591
01:09:00.300 --> 01:09:00.600
Woo-hoo!
呜呼！

1592
01:09:01.480 --> 01:09:03.080
Yay, Angela!
耶，安吉拉！

1593
01:09:03.420 --> 01:09:03.680
Yay!
耶！

1594
01:09:03.680 --> 01:09:07.920
Next time I talk to you guys, I'll be American surveyed, 50 to 75.
下次和你们聊天时，我就要参加美国人口普查了，50到75岁那组。

1595
01:09:08.300 --> 01:09:08.840
That'll be me.
那就是我了。

1596
01:09:11.020 --> 01:09:12.260
See you next week.
下周见。

1597
01:09:12.400 --> 01:09:12.660
Bye!
再见！

1598
01:09:16.020 --> 01:09:18.700
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies' Second Drink.
感谢收听《办公室女士》的“第二杯酒”。

